WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.472
Clima Protect makes rainfall-based protection transparent,

2
00:00:02.472 --> 00:00:07.004
from the terms you choose to a result you can verify.

3
00:00:07.004 --> 00:00:09.063
This is the Nimbus prototype.

4
00:00:09.063 --> 00:00:12.771
Let's go from rainfall evidence to the quote screen.

5
00:00:14.426 --> 00:00:17.247
Start with Nairobi and a fourteen-day window.

6
00:00:17.247 --> 00:00:22.082
Choose how rainfall is aggregated, set the threshold, and
replay the archive.

7
00:00:22.082 --> 00:00:26.111
Fourteen daily readings add up to four point six
millimetres,

8
00:00:26.111 --> 00:00:28.126
meeting the selected drought trigger.

9
00:00:31.399 --> 00:00:35.029
Change the threshold to three millimetres and replay.

10
00:00:35.029 --> 00:00:40.021
The weather hasn't changed, but the trigger is no longer
met.

11
00:00:40.021 --> 00:00:44.105
Put the original terms back, and the result returns.

12
00:00:44.105 --> 00:00:47.282
Compare policy settings against the same evidence.

13
00:00:47.715 --> 00:00:49.302
Open the provenance panel.

14
00:00:49.302 --> 00:00:52.477
The model, coordinates and daily readings are visible.

15
00:00:52.477 --> 00:00:56.842
The receipt binds them to the policy terms and calculated
outcome.

16
00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:00.811
Download it, and anyone can check the same result
independently.

17
00:01:03.148 --> 00:01:05.734
Import the receipt we just exported.

18
00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:09.180
The verifier reconstructs the calculation and confirms it.

19
00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.489
Now import an altered result, even with a recalculated
hash.

20
00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:14.782
It is rejected.

21
00:01:14.782 --> 00:01:18.659
Verification goes beyond checking whether a file has
changed.

22
00:01:20.525 --> 00:01:23.629
Take those verified terms into policy setup.

23
00:01:23.629 --> 00:01:27.619
The region, index, window, threshold and payout carry
forward.

24
00:01:27.619 --> 00:01:31.167
Step through the configuration and request a quote.

25
00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:34.271
The prototype produces a reviewable policy summary.

26
00:01:34.984 --> 00:01:38.832
The underlying Solana flow has also been exercised

27
00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:41.717
from pooled liquidity and signed purchase

28
00:01:41.717 --> 00:01:44.121
through triggered and non-triggered settlement.

29
00:01:44.121 --> 00:01:46.526
Clima Protect connects configurable terms,

30
00:01:46.526 --> 00:01:49.892
reproducible outcomes and receipts people can verify.
